## What to return
A JSON object carrying "body" and "commitments". Both are strings and nothing else is required.

To ground a claim, add a citation naming a block and quoting its own words, like this:
  "citations": [{"block": "0ff83bd21bd273ba", "quote": "<words copied from that block>"}]

## The shape this answer must take
`commitments` must be a STRING whose content is JSON text fitting exactly this schema (the field itself is a string, not an object):
{
  "properties": {
    "input": {
      "pattern": "^(\\{[\\s\\S]*\\}|[A-Za-z][^{}]{2,160}[.!?])$",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "kernel": {
      "pattern": "^conformance\\.kernel\\.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "transform": {
      "pattern": "^conformance\\.transform\\.",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "kernel",
    "transform",
    "input"
  ],
  "type": "object"
}